  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q105-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Simplify $\\operatorname{cosec}(n\\pi+\\theta)$ for integer $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(-1)^n\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta$, where $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$.\n\nUse reciprocal sine and distinguish even and odd $n$.",
      "worked": "For even $n$, $\\sin(n\\pi+\\theta)=\\sin\\theta$; for odd $n$, $\\sin(n\\pi+\\theta)=-\\sin\\theta$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{cosec}(n\\pi+\\theta)&=\\frac{1}{\\sin(n\\pi+\\theta)}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(n\\pi+\\theta)&=\\frac{1}{(-1)^n\\sin\\theta}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}(n\\pi+\\theta)&=(-1)^n\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth expressions are defined when $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 46
  },
